# Jenkins Chained Builds: Automated Git Deployment & Service Management

## Overview
Configured an automated two-stage CI/CD pipeline in **Jenkins** using chained upstream/downstream jobs to deploy updates from a Git repository onto **App Server 1 (`stapp01`)** and restart the Apache web server (`httpd`).

- **Upstream Job (`nautilus-app-deployment`):** Connects via SSH to `tony@stapp01`, checks out the `master` branch under `/var/www/html`, and pulls the latest commits.
- **Downstream Job (`manage-services`):** Automatically triggered only when `nautilus-app-deployment` succeeds (`SUCCESS`), connecting to `tony@stapp01` to restart the `httpd` service.

