## Implementation Steps & Commands

### 1. Configure Passwordless SSH from `jenkins` Service User to `tony@stapp01`
Generated an RSA key in PEM format directly under the `jenkins` user (`/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/id_rsa`) and authorized it on App Server 1:

```bash
ssh jenkins@jenkins
ssh-keygen -t rsa -m PEM -N "" -f ~/.ssh/id_rsa
ssh-copy-id -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no tony@stapp01
2. Clean Job Configurations via CLI (config.xml)Removed broken SSH Agent <buildWrappers> entries and ensured exact shell commands were configured in both job XML files on the Jenkins controller:Bash# Remove legacy SSH Agent wrappers from both jobs
sed -i '/<buildWrappers>/,/<\/buildWrappers>/c\<buildWrappers/>' /var/lib/jenkins/jobs/*/config.xml

# Set exact Git deployment command in nautilus-app-deployment
sed -i 's|sudo systemctl restart httpd|cd /var/www/html \&amp;\&amp; sudo git checkout master \&amp;\&amp; sudo git pull origin master|' /var/lib/jenkins/jobs/nautilus-app-deployment/config.xml

# Verify commands across both job configs
grep "<command>" /var/lib/jenkins/jobs/*/config.xml
3. Reload Jenkins Configuration & Trigger Chained Builds via REST API (with CSRF Crumb)Fetched a valid Jenkins CSRF crumb and session cookie to reload configuration from disk and execute two consecutive verification runs:BashCRUMB=$(curl -s -c /tmp/cookies -u 'admin:Adm!n321' 'http://localhost:8080/crumbIssuer/api/xml?xpath=concat(//crumbRequestField,":",//crumb)')

# Reload Jenkins configuration from disk
curl -s -b /tmp/cookies -u 'admin:Adm!n321' -H "$CRUMB" -X POST http://localhost:8080/reload && sleep 4

# Trigger Run #1 and Run #2
curl -s -b /tmp/cookies -u 'admin:Adm!n321' -H "$CRUMB" -X POST http://localhost:8080/job/nautilus-app-deployment/build && sleep 8
curl -s -b /tmp/cookies -u 'admin:Adm!n321' -H "$CRUMB" -X POST http://localhost:8080/job/nautilus-app-deployment/build && sleep 8
